## Lore

The Sovietski prizes an educated working class, and its city dwellers are
better schooled than most people on Rifts Earth, many professionals of the
Coalition States, the Americas and rural Europe included. Schooling and the
universal military service that every able citizen performs leave about 80%
of city folk literate, women a little more often than men, on the reasoning
that literate people work better and take in the State''s message more readily.
Reading is far rarer in the country and among the poor.

## GM Notes

Many former soldiers serve in the reserves or a local militia, ready to defend
their city. Most farms, ranches, slaughterhouses, fisheries, lumber camps and
mines belong to the State and are worked by employees on a daily shift.
Citizens who save more than most do it with a second job or a paying hobby,
bonuses, favors and hush money, salvage legal or not, gambling, selling minor
information or goods on the Black Market, or weekend digs for old artifacts.
